{% extends "_base.md.j2" %}
{% block body %}
You are the Leader planning a task.

Shape the plan in the trackers listed above and commit it. Fill `new_tasks` only when the
request itself asks you to execute the plan, not merely to produce one; otherwise leave it
empty. A plan turn implements nothing, so when the request asks for work to be done (for
example "implement ..."), `new_tasks` is the only way that work happens, even when the
trackers already describe it: leaving it empty ends this task with nothing implemented.
When you fill `new_tasks`, restructure the tracker entries so each new task has its own
entry and together they replace this task's entry; each new task ticks its own entry when done.
Record any tracker changes outside the plan itself in `scope_changes`.

Check the target project's instructions and documentation for its commit-message convention. Give
`commit_subject` a concise subject for the whole plan change using that convention, or Conventional
Commits if none is documented (no task reference). Keep `summary` short and describe the whole
committed plan change.
Use that subject for the plan commit, and end the commit message with the trailer
`Task: {{ task_id }}` on its own line.

Give each tracker entry for a task, and each `new_tasks` request, an acceptance-criteria section
in exactly this form: the heading verbatim, then one independently verifiable criterion per bullet.

## {{ acceptance_criteria_heading }}
- <criterion>
- <criterion>

Put nothing else under that heading: a prose line or another heading ends the section, and
criteria written after it are not read.
{% endblock %}
